{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"k-clique communities by clique percolation (Palla, Derényi, Farkas and Vicsek 2005): the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"unions of k-cliques that can be reached from one another through k-cliques sharing k − 1"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertices. Communities can overlap, and a vertex in no k-clique is in none. Computed from the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"maximal cliques of at least k vertices ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maximalCliques()"},{"type":"text","text":"), two joined when they share at"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"least k − 1 vertices. Self-loops and parallel edges are ignored."}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/CommunityDetection\/documentation\/CommunityDetection","doc:\/\/CommunityDetection\/documentation\/CommunityDetection\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/CommunityDetection\/documentation\/CommunityDetection\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"kCliqueCommunities","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"_","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"k","kind":"internalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> [[","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"]]","kind":"text"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"kind":"parameters","parameters":[{"name":"k","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The clique size, at least 2 (k = 2 gives the components with an edge).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"return-value","